"""Classic bedtime tales, retold gently for Storytime.

Each entry is my own retelling of a tale whose original text is in the public
domain. British English, short sentences, calm endings. The frightening parts
are softened: nobody is eaten or burned in these pages, and every story ends
quietly ready for sleep.

Reading speed: measured from 84 real Storytime stories on the household server
(words and seconds of the finished audio). The current reader speaks at a
median of 146 words per minute, between 134 and 166. I use 140 words per minute
as a calm read-aloud pace, so a tale of 840 to 1400 words lasts 6 to 10 minutes.
"""

READ_ALOUD_WPM = 140
MIN_WORDS = READ_ALOUD_WPM * 6
MAX_WORDS = READ_ALOUD_WPM * 10

